  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="a9620f5c-7c91-5ed2-b4cd-0f92cb3d6630" activityNameId="587114b7-b2b1-5d5f-bd8a-ab9bd416c03b" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Chlorine, gaseous, mercury cell, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Chlorine, gaseous, mercury cell, at plant
The multioutput-process "chlor-alkali electrolysis, mercury cell" delivers the co-products "chlorine, gaseous, mercury cell, at plant", "sodium hydroxide, 50% in water, mercury cell, at plant" and "hydrogen, liquid, mercury cell, at plant". The allocation is done according to the masses of the different products - i.e. 46.4% chlorine - 52.3% sodium hydroxide and 1.3% hydrogen.;
UUID: 5e03106d-1cf4-3e27-9461-9bdd7630a127
Besides the electrolysis process in a mercury cell, the following process steps are included into this process: brine production, brine purification, brine resaturation as well as the final handling of the electrolysis products, without the chlorine liquifaction!
Location: European average values
Technology: present state of technology used in european mercury cells
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Average values from the ranges indicated in EC IPPC-BAT document are used 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: &lt;null&gt;
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_5e03106d-1cf4-3e27-9461-9bdd7630a127.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
